      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While sub-audible frequency transmission via power lines is theoretically possible in laboratory settings, no credible evidence suggests that standard smart bulbs or thermostats are recording and transmitting your private conversations in this manner. The consistency of your observation likely stems from psychological factors or an unrelated electrical interference that you are unconsciously linking to your specific conversations. It is highly improbable that these devices have the necessary software capabilities to coordinate audio capture through electrical signals, and seeking a professional technician to check for wiring faults or device incompatibility is the most practical step for your peace of mind.",
